  "text": "On an average day in 1998, statistician David Fairley was walking up a busy San Francisco street to pick up his son from preschool. Traffic was heavy, and halfway to the school, he started to feel weak and dazed.\n\n\"Actually, a homeless guy saw me and helped me to the school,\" Fairley said. \"[People at the school] had me lie down for a bit.\"\n\nFairley felt better after a rest, but the school administrators insisted he go to the hospital. On the way there, he had a heart attack.\n\nIt's not necessarily enough to have all the information... we need to have the right information in the precise moment in which we are making a decision.",
